  "findings": [
    "The flag predicate exactly matches the unchanged resolver quote-trimmed ASCII-case-folded Courier/monospace/Monospaced set. Every tested member retains the flag with nested bold/size/color; Courier New, mono, DialogInput, Lucida Console, Serif, Dialog and SansSerif do not gain that flag. Courier New uses its preexisting dedicated CourierNew metric family, not the compatibility flag.",
    "The word trimmed must be qualified. Rust trims quotes only; it does not trim whitespace. FontStack.getFonts uses trimWhitespaceOrDoubleQuote before Font.decode. Quoted padded monospace and trailing-space Courier therefore are not Rust aliases although Java metrics trim them. The maker account explicitly limits compatibility to the existing resolver normalization; it does not establish Java whitespace-normalized family parity. A padded family is also not normalized for Java SVG NBSP selection, which compares the preserved string.",
    "Unpadded Courier preserves the Mono metric branch. Monospace/Monospaced set the flag but text_render explicit_monospace_font_uses_surrounding_metrics chooses surrounding metrics; the flag is not evidence that a monospaced metric table was selected. The restored Monospaced metric difference is real and reproduced. No shared resolver change was made.",
    "Fresh alias whole outputs: 2 to4 passes /12 valid observations. COURIER and MONOSPACE controls remain passing; mono and Lucida Console improve. Quoted padding, trailing spaces, logical families, mixed size baselines and note height produce failures. Whole-output rule rejects this mechanism despite restored compatibility flags.",
    "Six separate golden controls reproduce6 to0 to6 actual CLI passes: activity/act_creole_monospace and creole/creole_font_name_in_activity,class,note,sequence,title. All six source hashes are absent from every1992 replay membership. They were found by the first draft broad unit/library gates, not its replay or focused creole-only membership; this is an explicit replay-coverage finding.",
    "Independent initial product diagnostics reproduce11173/11251 (six lost baseline names) and assisted10492/11251 (five lost names, note excluded). Final product11179 and assisted10497 reproduce; their72/754 failure-name files are byte-identical to both the freshly built baseline and maker baseline. All six extra YAML models are byte-equal before/initial/final.",
    "Java provenance is CommandCreoleFontFamilyChange.executeAndGetRemaining -> FontConfiguration.changeFamily preserving face/size -> FontStack.getFonts/Font.decode -> UFontImpl.getFamily(SVG) and SvgGraphics697-708 logical-name/NBSP handling. The production alias predicate does not change font assets or geometry and does not add aliases."
  ],
